{"i":3,"out":"{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kwas3","path":"packages/storage/src/store.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yvAFD","body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Guard recovery cleanup against concurrent store writers**\n\nWhen another Diffpanel command opens the same home while `createPreparedRun()` is between creating its run directory and inserting the database row, this recovery loop classifies that active directory as orphaned and recursively deletes it. This is particularly likely while the VS Code extension polls `list` every few seconds, because every `DiffpanelStore.open()` now runs recovery; the preparing command can then fail while writing its manifest or commit a run whose newly written blobs were removed by the subsequent garbage collection. Recovery and creation need interprocess coordination or a staging scheme that distinguishes active writes from abandoned data.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","outdated":false,"url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4072407363","author":"chatgpt-codex-connector"}]}
{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kwas9","path":"packages/git/src/capture.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yvAFO","body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Propagate bounded Git failures instead of returning missing content**\n\nWhen `git show` is cancelled, times out, or exceeds `maxProcessOutputBytes`, the newly passed process options cause `gitBuffer` to throw, but this catch converts every such failure into a legitimate absent blob. For example, a staged or range change to a binary larger than the default 16 MiB output cap produces `null` for both sides and can be recorded as a metadata-only review item rather than being skipped as binary/oversized, yielding an incomplete immutable snapshot. Only Git's expected missing-object case should return `null`; limit, timeout, and cancellation errors must propagate.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","outdated":true,"url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4072407374","author":"chatgpt-codex-connector"}]}
