{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kyFoy","path":"packages/storage/src/store.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yxg0Q","body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid full integrity recovery on every store open**\n\nWhen the library contains large snapshots, the VS Code provider polls `list` every four seconds (`apps/vscode/src/tree.ts:20-22`), and every resulting CLI process reaches this call before it can answer. `recover()` takes an exclusive `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` lock, reads and hashes every referenced blob in every run, and scans the blob tree for garbage; pagination repeats that work in a separate process for each page. Once this scan takes longer than the polling interval, list processes accumulate while prep and publish wait on the writer lock, making the extension and CLI progressively unusable. Gate the expensive integrity/GC pass behind explicit or infrequent maintenance rather than running it for every read command.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","outdated":true,"url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4073065744","author":"chatgpt-codex-connector"}]}
{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kyFo7","path":"packages/storage/src/store.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yxg0a","body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep filesystem deletion outside the rollback scope**\n\nIf pruning encounters an error after one of these `rm` calls, the outer maintenance transaction rolls the database deletions back but cannot restore the run directories already removed. A concrete case is repository-scoped pruning when another repository has an unreadable retained manifest: the scoped preflight succeeds, these directories are deleted, then the global `garbageCollectBlobsLocked()` fails on that unrelated manifest, restoring rows whose manifests and reviews no longer exist. Preflight all potentially failing global work before deletion, or commit the row removal before performing idempotent filesystem cleanup.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.","outdated":true,"url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4073065754","author":"chatgpt-codex-connector"}]}
