{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kwas3","path":"packages/storage/src/store.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yvAFD","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4072407363","outdated":false,"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Guard recovery cleanup against concurrent store writers**  When another Diffpanel command opens the same home while `createPreparedRun()` is between creating its run directory and inserting the database row, this recovery loop classifies that active directory as orphaned and recursively deletes it. This is particularly likely while the VS Code extension polls `list` every few seconds, because every `DiffpanelStore.open()` now runs recovery; the preparing command can then fail while writing its manifest or commit a run whose newly written blobs were removed by the subsequent garbage collection. Recovery and creation need interprocess coordination or a staging scheme that distinguishes active writes from abandoned data.  Useful? React with 👍 / 👎."}]}
