{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kwas9","path":"packages/git/src/capture.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yvAFO","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4072407374","outdated":true,"body":"**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Propagate bounded Git failures instead of returning missing content**  When `git show` is cancelled, times out, or exceeds `maxProcessOutputBytes`, the newly passed process options cause `gitBuffer` to throw, but this catch converts every such failure into a legitimate absent blob. For example, a staged or range change to a binary larger than the default 16 MiB output cap produces `null` for both sides and can be recorded as a metadata-only review item rather than being skipped as binary/oversized, yielding an incomplete immutable snapshot. Only Git's expected missing-object case should return `null`; limit, timeout, and cancellation errors must propagate.  Useful? React with 👍 / 👎."}]}
{"id":"PRRT_kwDOTzN9qc6kwatD","path":"apps/cli/src/index.ts","comments":[{"id":"PRRC_kwDOTzN9qc7yvAFW","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/diffpanel/pull/1#discussion_r4072407382","outdated":true,"body":"**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Paginate the extension before capping list output**  Once a library has more than 50 matching runs, the VS Code client still invokes `list --json` without `--page`, `--limit`, or a cursor, so this new default silently returns only the newest 50 and older reviews disappear from both the normal and archived trees. Preserve exhaustive output for the legacy JSON invocation or update `apps/vscode/src/cli.ts` to request pages until `nextCursor` is null.  Useful? React with 👍 / 👎."}]}
